{%- comment -%}
  About Us. Brief §13: "About page dibuat singkat dan visual" — short and
  visual, and explicitly "tidak perlu terlalu corporate". So this is one
  section, not a page of them: a photograph, a heading, and one paragraph.

  THE FOUR FACTS ARE THE BRIEF'S OWN, AND NOTHING IS ADDED TO THEM. §13 gives
  exactly four: founded 2020, an Indonesian womenswear label, comfortable /
  versatile / wearable as the focus, and custom apparel production alongside
  ready-to-wear. PRODUCT.md lists "About Us history, founder or team facts,
  production volumes" under things not to fabricate — so there is no founder
  name, no team size, no "since 2020 we've dressed thousands of women" here,
  and there should not be one added later without the studio supplying it.

  THE HEADING IS THE BRIEF'S OWN LINE, not an invented one — §6's hero
  example, "Everyday Pieces, Made for You." It was never used when the home
  hero became a film with no copy at all (see hero-video.liquid), so this is
  the first place on the live site it appears rather than a duplicate.

  THE PHOTOGRAPH DEFAULTS TO `door-shop.webp`, RATHER THAN A PLACEHOLDER. It
  is the square crop of the polaroid composition that led the old hero
  carousel, and it has stood unreferenced since two-ways.liquid dropped its
  photography 2026-09-21 (see that section's own comment) — reusing it here
  answers the brief's "visual" ask with an asset that already exists instead
  of waiting on a new shoot for a page whose brief explicitly asks for
  "singkat", not a campaign. An image uploaded in the theme editor overrides
  it, same precedence as `media-asset` everywhere else.

  NO CTA. A "Shop now" button here would make this page compete with the
  hero and the two-ways doors that already carry that job. About's only job
  is the four facts above, believably told.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-content flex-col gap-8 px-gutter pb-section pt-block-lg sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:gap-12 lg:gap-16">
  <div data-reveal class="sm:w-[42%] sm:shrink-0">
    {% render 'media-asset',
      image: section.settings.image,
      asset: 'door-shop.webp',
      alt: "A square crop of Wear Label's ready-to-wear polaroid campaign.",
      ratio: '1 / 1',
      sizes: '(min-width: 640px) 42vw, 100vw',
      asset_width: 1100,
      asset_height: 1100,
      label: 'Studio photo' %}
  </div>

  <div data-reveal class="wl-measure flex flex-col gap-4">
    <span class="text-micro uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-ink-subtle">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.eyebrow, label: 'eyebrow', inline: true %}
    </span>

    <h1 class="text-h1 leading-h1">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'heading', lines: 2 %}
    </h1>

    <p class="text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.body, label: 'body', lines: 3 %}
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "About story",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Brief §13: short and visual, not corporate. Only the four facts the brief itself gives — founding year, what Wear Label is, what it focuses on, and the custom-apparel side — belong here. No founder, team or volume claim the studio has not supplied." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "About Wear Label" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Everyday Pieces, Made for You." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body", "default": "Wear Label is an Indonesian womenswear label, founded in 2020 around one idea: clothes should be comfortable enough for every day and versatile enough to wear again and again. Alongside our ready-to-wear collection, we also produce custom apparel — uniforms, merchandise and special projects for companies, schools, and organizations." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photograph", "info": "Overrides the shipped door-shop.webp default." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "About story" }]
}
{% endschema %}
